From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 04:04:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: Add Exynos9820 power domain

Exynos9820 uses the same power domain block as the older Exynos SoCs and
the same node layout, so the binding only gains a compatible. The driver
does need its own entry, because the enable mask differs from every
existing one, and that comes in the next patch.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/pd-samsung.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/pd-samsung.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/pd-samsung.yaml
index 9c2c5113345..d3a3c4a30cf 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/pd-samsung.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/pd-samsung.yaml
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ properties:
     enum:
       - samsung,exynos4210-pd
       - samsung,exynos5433-pd
+      - samsung,exynos9820-pd
 
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
